  "content": {
    "id": "teacher-p35-q22-bridge-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "",
    "prompt": "Each expression below has four terms and no bracket is showing yet. You can create a shared bracket by pairing the terms. Take a common factor out of each pair so that the same bracket appears in both. When a pair starts with a negative term, take out a negative factor, for example $-3m-6=-3(m+2)$. Then take out the shared bracket and use the difference of two squares to factorise fully.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "teacher-p35-q22-bridge-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^3+3x^2-4x-12$\n\nPair the terms as $(x^3+3x^2)+(-4x-12)$. Complete the pairing, then take out the shared bracket and factorise fully:\n\n$x^3+3x^2-4x-12=x^2(\\hspace{15mm}\\rule{0pt}{2ex})-4(\\hspace{15mm}\\rule{0pt}{2ex})$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+3)(x-2)(x+2)$",
          "worked": "$\\begin{align*}x^3+3x^2-4x-12&=x^2(x+3)-4(x+3)\\\\&=(x+3)(x^2-4)\\\\&=(x+3)(x-2)(x+2)\\end{align*}$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      },
      {
        "id": "teacher-p35-q22-bridge-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$k^6-4k^4-k^2+4$\n\nThe pairs are $(k^6-4k^4)+(-k^2+4)$. Make a shared bracket from them, taking out a negative factor from the second pair. Then factorise fully.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(k-2)(k+2)(k-1)(k+1)(k^2+1)$",
          "worked": "$\\begin{align*}k^6-4k^4-k^2+4&=k^4(k^2-4)-1(k^2-4)\\\\&=(k^2-4)(k^4-1)\\\\&=(k^2-4)(k^2-1)(k^2+1)\\\\&=(k-2)(k+2)(k-1)(k+1)(k^2+1)\\end{align*}$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p35-q22-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$w^6-w^4-w^2+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(w-1)^2(w+1)^2(w^2+1)$",
          "worked": "$\\begin{align*}w^6-w^4-w^2+1&=w^4(w^2-1)-(w^2-1)\\\\&=(w^2-1)(w^4-1)\\\\&=(w^2-1)^2(w^2+1)\\\\&=(w-1)^2(w+1)^2(w^2+1)\\end{align*}$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      }
    ]
  },
